{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog","id":1073083,"title":"The Autumn Court (Open Development Blog)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-04T06:41:09-07:00","id":1073083,"title":"The Autumn Court (Open Development Blog)","content":"So, look what I found just sitting in the announcements section. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-autumn-court-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">It's a brand new Changeling blog!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:23:12-07:00","id":1073105,"title":"","content":"It seems like the Court System has seen major changes. <br /> <br /> The flavour of the Autumn Court is excellent, but I saw nothing about approaches, but something about Bargains instead and forcing the Gentry into attacking transparently. <br /> <br /> It appears the Court Systems have been heavily modified from David Hills vision of it, but so far I'm intrigued. I just hope the Scheherazade's Freehold remains.<br /> <br /> I'll add that if approaches are gone, that not only does that mean a radically redesign of courts, but that huntsmen may have been radically redesigned as well, if they are even a thing anymore, which they might not be. <br /> <br /> I just don't have enough Intel to know what to think aside from really liking the Autumn Courts flavour. <br /> <br /> I assume Honshu Freehold is still in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-04-2017, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:31:31-07:00","id":1073110,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm really hoping that Honshu and Toronto made it in mostly unscathed. Too many unknowns to know for sure right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:33:02-07:00","id":1073111,"title":"","content":"Paris too, Arc put a lot of effort into his Paris Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:34:27-07:00","id":1073112,"title":"","content":"Hmm, is Bargaining and Give And Take the new terms for Approaches? It does make sense; you propose to give the Huntsmen this thing, in return for that other thing. Matches how Approaches work (or worked) by giving Yearning to Huntsmen, in return for making them behave according to expectations.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> After reading the Legends part, now I think that &quot;Bargaining&quot; is a narrative that Autumn expects his followers to comply by, if they want to keep her blessings. That blessing is probably concealment from the True Fae and their Huntsmen. Maybe the other Seasons (and other Court patrons) will have similar things they expect of their changelings, be they called &quot;Bargains&quot; or not. If they are called Bargains, however, then I wonder what happens to the type of Pledges that shares the same name.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Autumn in the Legends remind me of Izanami from Japanese mythology, and Demeter from Greek mythology (except gender-reversed in the latter case)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-04-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:46:27-07:00","id":1073122,"title":"","content":"Looks fine so far. I like the focus on rituals and superstitions.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping we get to see just what it means to be a sorcerer some time in the near-future, though, because, at the moment, Contracts are something every Court has and every Changeling does. Being called a sorcerer should mean something, so what's it going to mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:51:31-07:00","id":1073125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073122#post1073122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks fine so far. I like the focus on rituals and superstitions.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping we get to see just what it means to be a sorcerer some time in the near-future, though, because, at the moment, Contracts are something every Court has and every Changeling does. Being called a sorcerer should mean something, so what's it going to mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since fairy magic is primarily described as a form of bargaining (as this preview emphasizes), I suspect that Goblin Vows, Goblin Contracts, tokens, and even mundane things like extracting favors from other supernatural forces all count as sorcery. At least for the Fair Folk, that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:39:49-07:00","id":1073145,"title":"","content":"That seems like the sort of thing <i>every</i> Changeling does, though, which is the problem. All those things are things other Changelings do. If you can curse your enemies, bless your friends, turn invisible with a snap of your fingers, and make a deal with a thunderstorm to cover your escape, why are you going to think of someone else as a sorcerer for doing the exact same things but not call yourself the same?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:44:02-07:00","id":1073148,"title":"","content":"Give and Take appears to have replaces approaches. <br /> <br /> Give is whatever the Court made a deal with gives to the Changelings, and Take is what that Facet of the Wyrd gets in return. <br /> <br /> Example Give: Autumn gives the Freeholds Changelings transpancy when Autumn Rules, forcing the Gentry &amp; minions to offer warning before striking.<br /> <br /> Take: The Changelings of the Autumn Court conduct rituals as playment for Autumns support.<br /> <br /> I'm curious if Bulwark is even a thing now?<br /> <br /> I'll also note that the facet of the Wyrd or whatever Autumn is appears to have more personality then before, like being, not just a mindless force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:45:37-07:00","id":1073149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073145#post1073145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like the sort of thing <i>every</i> Changeling does, though, which is the problem. All those things are things other Changelings do. If you can curse your enemies, bless your friends, turn invisible with a snap of your fingers, and make a deal with a thunderstorm to cover your escape, why are you going to think of someone else as a sorcerer for doing the exact same things but not call yourself the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the same reason most of use don't get to call ourselves a scientist or an engineer, despite being proficient with modern technology and knowing some of the laws of physics on an intuitive level. <br /> <br /> It's about living the magic, not just using it. <br /> <br /> (And yet I'll be happy if my perspective is shot down with a sorcery system implemented for Changeling)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:46:49-07:00","id":1073150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073145#post1073145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like the sort of thing <i>every</i> Changeling does, though, which is the problem. All those things are things other Changelings do. If you can curse your enemies, bless your friends, turn invisible with a snap of your fingers, and make a deal with a thunderstorm to cover your escape, why are you going to think of someone else as a sorcerer for doing the exact same things but not call yourself the same?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think sorcerors is just a nickname for Autumn Courtiers emphasizing their obsession with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:02:22-07:00","id":1073161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073149#post1073149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the same reason most of use don't get to call ourselves a scientist or an engineer, despite being proficient with modern technology and knowing some of the laws of physics on an intuitive level.<br /> <br /> It's about living the magic, not just using it.<br /> <br /> (And yet I'll be happy if my perspective is shot down with a sorcery system implemented for Changeling)</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, though, <i>every</i> Changeling lives the magic. An Elemental walks out of the Hedge with a body that is a humanoid storm and feels kinship with every flash of lightning and rumble of thunder. What is that if not living the magic?<br /> <br /> I guess we'll both just have to hope that it does mean slightly more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073150#post1073150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think sorcerors is just a nickname for Autumn Courtiers emphasizing their obsession with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's all it is, colour me disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:09:25-07:00","id":1073166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073105#post1073105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll add that if approaches are gone, that not only does that mean a radically redesign of courts, but that huntsmen may have been radically redesigned as well, if they are even a thing anymore, which they might not be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The preview's opening suggests Huntsmen are still around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:24:57-07:00","id":1073176,"title":"","content":"No approaches, huh? Yeah, gonna stick to 1e for my next game till this confusion is sorted oit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:33:37-07:00","id":1073185,"title":"","content":"Why Autumn court are &quot;sorcerers&quot; and other Seasonal Courts aren't, based on 1e abilities.<br /> <br /> The mantles. Autumn gave bonus to occult rolls. Granted, it was wildly useless in a lot of cases, but that seems to have changed in 2e. Bonus to investigating anything related to the fae. The crown gained bonuses related to gathering secrets, including magic secrets. Their entire mantle encouraged studying fae magics. That alone made Autumn more sorcerous than anyone else, simply by virtue of their area of focus. Spring got social boons, Summer got physical, Winter got stealth.<br /> <br /> The Fleeting follow the same pattern as the mantle. Desire more often than not tied into granted social ability tied to making pledges; learning what a person wants, forcing them to do anything for that want, and then manifesting that want. Wrath allowed you to find or manipulate fights, both starting and stopping, or enhancing fighting skills. Fleeting Winter allowed you to be better at distracting so you could sneak. Fleeting autumn was magic attacks using fear, and creating shields against nightmares. As the only magic directly used in attack or defense rather than enhancing other skills, it gave a very sorcerous vibe compared to warriors and sneaks.<br /> <br /> Then, we had Spellbound Autumn, which directly hacked into things like Kenning, tokens, hobs and pledgecraft. Relatedly, Eternal Autumn 1 was excellent at harvesting goblin fruits.<br /> <br /> So, not only do we have better faculty with the supernatural (both in detecting it and knowing about it) but the combat and social abilities felt like you were acting like a sorcerer more than any thing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:38:55-07:00","id":1073191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073166#post1073166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The preview's opening suggests Huntsmen are still around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To the best of my knowledge, the focus of Changeling 2e is still &quot;The Huntsmen Chronicle.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:00:17-07:00","id":1073214,"title":"","content":"&quot;Other Court models are also in the core book. Every setting in Chapter 6 has its own Courts, each of which has its own Mantle. There are rules for making your own Bargains, Mantles, and Crowns in Chapter 7.&quot;<br /> <br /> That suggests to me Honshu and Scheherazade's Freehold are likely still in the book, but different now with Bargains and Crowns??? and perhaps changes to how mantle works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:17:14-07:00","id":1073229,"title":"","content":"It seems that we're dropping the story parts and adopting pact magic in its place. So, we're back to making deals with the five Directions, the Seasons and the Time of Day for Courts for defense against the Fae. <br /> <br /> So, Honshu and Tornoto could very well remain, but they're going to need something to Bargain with to hold on. At least the Scheherazade Freehold is pretty easy - at least two of the Courts there are collapsed versions of bigger systems living together. Seasonal and Directional. We could just continue with that in the same vein for the other Courts there. Bargains with seasonal, directions, etc as the whole.<br /> <br /> Honshu... I'm not sure how that would work now. Its pretty much based entirely on the Bamboo Cutter's Daughter legend, and I can't think of whom the pact would be with. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T11:23:20-07:00","id":1073270,"title":"","content":"Ah, my favorite of the four seasonal courts! I like it. Looking forward to Autumn's focus on magic being more concrete and eminently useful this time around.<br /> <br /> The write-up is interesting, but as others have said it does suggest some changes to the Freehold system. Or at least some heavy reframing? I'm not certain what's going on there. Things seem to have shifted from Approaches and the Bulwark as sustained by a narrative central to the freehold, but I can't tell how much it's just the take of the seasonal courts on it, and how much is actually different, because Give And Take seems to be about the Court Approach and with the Bulwark spread throughout.<br /> <br /> I'm afraid of being that guy who perceives a change that doesn't fit with his preference and runs off on an incomplete reading, getting his perspective prematurely tilted and unreceptive but - with that caveat in mind. I was very enthused over what was initially presented of the new freeholds and courts,with their workings leaning strongly towards the symbolism of legends and stories as the answer of the Lost to the Gentry and Huntsmen, using the same rules they cleave to for protection and to interact with faerie on their own terms, and I'm a little concerned that paradigm is getting toned down.<br /> <br /> After listening to that compelling vision of Freeholds and Courts, where each region has its unique ways and line-up of factions, I also can't say I would care as much for the seasonal courts being presented as the default again, especially since each setting is supposed to get an elaboration on their Courts and Freehold, but maybe I'm reacting too hard to this! I don't want to be negative or come off as a naysayer, but the thoughts nag me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-04-2017, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T11:53:24-07:00","id":1073285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073270#post1073270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After listening to that compelling vision of Freeholds and Courts, where each region has its unique ways and line-up of factions, I also can't say I would care as much for the seasonal courts being presented as the default again, especially since each setting is supposed to get an elaboration on their Courts and Freehold, but maybe I'm reacting too hard to this! I don't want to be negative or come off as a naysayer, but the thoughts nag me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same thought is nagging me. The seasonal courts were one of the biggest reasons I had trouble getting into Changeling and I was thrilled with the more global and local take that uncoupling the seasonal courts from being the default would have done. I feel like that nervousness will likely persist until we have the complete picture of what is changing in 2e. Not because I think the new team will do a poor job, I think it will be fantastic. Its the not know what's being changed, especially because David shared so much. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I am somewhat reassured by the Rose Courts from Dark Eras, since if I recall correctly, those were Rose's work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T12:02:42-07:00","id":1073292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073270#post1073270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid of being that guy who perceives a change that doesn't fit with his preference and runs off on an incomplete reading, getting his perspective prematurely tilted and unreceptive but - with that caveat in mind. I was very enthused over what was initially presented of the new freeholds and courts,with their workings leaning strongly towards the symbolism of legends and stories as the answer of the Lost to the Gentry and Huntsmen, using the same rules they cleave to for protection and to interact with faerie on their own terms, and I'm a little concerned that paradigm is getting toned down.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I'm fairly sure that the presence of a unifying feature of the Courts within a freehold is still present \u2014 Toronto's Silver Court working as it did being one of the more distinct implications that &quot;drawn from a story familiar to the locals&quot; is a very simplified explanation of the root of a Bulwark \u2014 and the Fae interaction with narrative has always been more of a consequence of their pseudomercantile existence than a cause of it; pactwork and exchange has a stronger fundamental basis for the fae than in-universe deep roleplaying.<br /> <br /> I could be biased, of course; this approach does make it a lot easier for me to frame Chicago's Courts of Wind and Fire without strictly binding the trolls and sprites of the city to the knock-on effects of century-old pop culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T12:07:58-07:00","id":1073294,"title":"","content":"Each setting (not all of the settings are strictly regional) has its own factions, and there's stuff to build your own. But we also present an exciting and accessible group of Courts in 1e-level detail, and those are the seasons.<br /> <br /> Starting with Vampire, there's been a pattern in 2e of encouraging factions unique to each setting while also presenting a set that are flavorful and easy to use in many settings, and Changeling follows that. As in other games, not all factions follow a single metaphysical model -- the French Market's Courts of exchange have some things in common with the seasons, but Hong Kong's factions are set up in an entirely different way. You'll find that the local Courts or other factions are closely tied in to the history of contact and conflict with faerie beings and phenomena in that particular area.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yes, Elizabethan London's Courts are a great example of 2e-style Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-04-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T12:12:41-07:00","id":1073298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073294#post1073294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You'll find that the local Courts or other factions are closely tied in to the history of contact and conflict with faerie beings and phenomena in that particular area.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is both enlightening and good to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T12:18:56-07:00","id":1073300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073294#post1073294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each setting (not all of the settings are strictly regional) has its own factions, and there's stuff to build your own. But we also present an exciting and accessible group of Courts in 1e-level detail, and those are the seasons.<br /> <br /> Starting with Vampire, there's been a pattern in 2e of encouraging factions unique to each setting while also presenting a set that are flavorful and easy to use in many settings, and Changeling follows that. As in other games, not all factions follow a single metaphysical model -- the French Market's Courts of exchange have some things in common with the seasons, but Hong Kong's factions are set up in an entirely different way. You'll find that the local Courts or other factions are closely tied in to the history of contact and conflict with faerie beings and phenomena in that particular area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Rose. That helps put my mind at ease a bit. Looking forward to seeing the new locales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T12:32:05-07:00","id":1073306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073292#post1073292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I'm fairly sure that the presence of a unifying feature of the Courts within a freehold is still present \u2014 Toronto's Silver Court working as it did being one of the more distinct implications that &quot;drawn from a story familiar to the locals&quot; is a very simplified explanation of the root of a Bulwark \u2014 and the Fae interaction with narrative has always been more of a consequence of their pseudomercantile existence than a cause of it; pactwork and exchange has a stronger fundamental basis for the fae than in-universe deep roleplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pactwork is certainly a very compelling path to focus on for the subject on its own. When you put it like that it alleviates some stress from my run-on trains of thought, though I was never worried it would be entirely withdrawn, since narrative symbolism looks inextricable from broad faerie dealings whether as a matter of fact or a ramification of their nature.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Thanks for the pertinent response, Rose! That's reassuring and leaves me looking forward to details and the new settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-04-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T12:42:27-07:00","id":1073310,"title":"","content":"Fairy tales play out in the Chronicles of Darkness because the setting has all the elements of a fairy tale world, not because there's a force that makes things conform.<br /> <br /> (Of course, the Gentry _do_ plagiarize ideas from humans... but they and other faerie beings and weird corners of history and clever soldiers and wise princesses and witches with chicken-legged huts are the sources of many of those ideas, too.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T13:08:31-07:00","id":1073322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073294#post1073294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each setting (not all of the settings are strictly regional) has its own factions, and there's stuff to build your own. But we also present an exciting and accessible group of Courts in 1e-level detail, and those are the seasons.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yes, Elizabethan London's Courts are a great example of 2e-style Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm most great full for Seasonal Courts being basic example - I sorta like that you can create your own Courts for special needs ( like I would use Native Americans Courts in New England ) but I would still like maybe 80% use Seasonal in my games, I really like them as they are. I will probably made my Changeling games about two Court systems fighting over community, like I plan to use Seasonal and Day/Night Courts in Lublin, Poland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-05-2017, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T13:11:19-07:00","id":1073325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073285#post1073285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not because I think the new team will do a poor job, I think it will be fantastic. Its the not know what's being changed, especially because David shared so much. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I am somewhat reassured by the Rose Courts from Dark Eras, since if I recall correctly, those were Rose's work.</div> </div> </div> </div> This, no disrespect is intended to Rose, I worry she will be offended by our concerns, but that is not my intent as I have the highest respect for Rose and her team their creative powers, but it just as you say that uncertainty as to what survived and did not survive the transition. It's the knowing and then not knowing that causes the nervousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T13:29:44-07:00","id":1073333,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's definitely putting me through a loop having seen so much of David's Lost, playing it, growing attached to it, and now not knowing what from it will still be present in Rose's Lost. That's by no means a knock against Rose's Lost, I'm sure it will be great. But being unsure how much of David's Lost's DNA it will share is naturally going to leave me a little anxious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T14:01:00-07:00","id":1073349,"title":"","content":"I say this not to be confrontational, but just to express a difference of opinion: I didn't like some of the directions Changeling 2e was going in. I'm feeling more hopeful. Vampire 2e was what actually made me <i>like</i> Vampire instead of feeling eternally put-off by it.<br /> <br /> Colour me curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T14:14:58-07:00","id":1073357,"title":"","content":"i enjoyed this incarnation of the autumn court more than i did before,and i absotuly loved autumn in 1e.<br /> I noticed the word Bargain is capitalized,is that Bargain something all courts have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T14:35:01-07:00","id":1073368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073322#post1073322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I'm most great full for Seasonal Courts being basic example - I sorta like that you can create your own Courts for special needs ( like I would use Native Americans Courts in New England ) but I would still like maybe 80% use Seasonal in my games, I really like them as they are. I will probably made my Changeling games about two Court systems fighting over community, like I plan to use Seasonal and Day/Night Courts in Lublin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that, most importantly, there need to be an example of &quot;real&quot;, playable setting, so you can pick up the game and play it. Accessability is extremely important if you want new people to try out the game, and it's IMHO unrealistic to expect people to create good &quot;do it on your own&quot; settings without having a good example to trace, dissect and learn from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T15:41:06-07:00","id":1073401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073368#post1073368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, most importantly, there need to be an example of &quot;real&quot;, playable setting, so you can pick up the game and play it. Accessability is extremely important if you want new people to try out the game, and it's IMHO unrealistic to expect people to create good &quot;do it on your own&quot; settings without having a good example to trace, dissect and learn from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has been a bit of an issue for my own custom freehold; I've got the concepts down, but without complete, almost official examples, it's difficult for me to finalize the courts overall within it. It'll be different from the seasonal courts, but having that kind of precedent will still set a lot of groundwork cut out for me without having to measure everything out first before I glue it together.<br /> <br /> ...that metaphor kind of got away from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T16:07:07-07:00","id":1073411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073294#post1073294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each setting (not all of the settings are strictly regional) has its own factions, and there's stuff to build your own. But we also present an exciting and accessible group of Courts in 1e-level detail, and those are the seasons.<br /> <br /> Starting with Vampire, there's been a pattern in 2e of encouraging factions unique to each setting while also presenting a set that are flavorful and easy to use in many settings, and Changeling follows that. As in other games, not all factions follow a single metaphysical model -- the French Market's Courts of exchange have some things in common with the seasons, but Hong Kong's factions are set up in an entirely different way. You'll find that the local Courts or other factions are closely tied in to the history of contact and conflict with faerie beings and phenomena in that particular area.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yes, Elizabethan London's Courts are a great example of 2e-style Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to take this as a yes Honsue and Toronto Freeholds are still in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T16:26:21-07:00","id":1073423,"title":"","content":"Do mantles no longer have benefits aside from aesthetics?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073368#post1073368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, most importantly, there need to be an example of &quot;real&quot;, playable setting, so you can pick up the game and play it. Accessability is extremely important if you want new people to try out the game, and it's IMHO unrealistic to expect people to create good &quot;do it on your own&quot; settings without having a good example to trace, dissect and learn from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was already present though, they were in the settings section (and we were even previewed the japan setting which had all the court details).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T16:41:10-07:00","id":1073428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073423#post1073423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was already present though, they were in the settings section (and we were even previewed the japan setting which had all the court details).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Here are the specific separate mystical organizational structures of this city, this city, and this region&quot; is not actually the same thing as &quot;Here's a Court structure that is common throughout a large part of the world, which you can adjust to better fit your particular setting.&quot; Honshu and Toronto don't help new players who want to set their game in Seattle or Raleigh without fairly extensive homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T16:54:45-07:00","id":1073431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073428#post1073428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Here are the specific separate mystical organizational structures of this city, this city, and this region&quot; is not actually the same thing as &quot;Here's a Court structure that is common throughout a large part of the world, which you can adjust to better fit your particular setting.&quot; Honshu and Toronto don't help new players who want to set their game in Seattle or Raleigh without fairly extensive homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't we told that Miami will have the Seasonal Court, specifically so that players who prefer the seasonal court can still just plug and play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-04-2017, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T16:59:18-07:00","id":1073434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073431#post1073431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't we told that Miami will have the Seasonal Court?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T16:59:21-07:00","id":1073435,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, the Seasonal Courts were always going to be included in the book as example Courts. They weren't in the playtestable chunks, presumably because they're not really essential to playtest the game, and not including them both leaves something to look forward to in the actual release and also encourages folks who want to playtest to put the Freehold creation rules through their paces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:08:45-07:00","id":1073441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073368#post1073368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, most importantly, there need to be an example of &quot;real&quot;, playable setting, so you can pick up the game and play it. Accessability is extremely important if you want new people to try out the game, and it's IMHO unrealistic to expect people to create good &quot;do it on your own&quot; settings without having a good example to trace, dissect and learn from.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, we were (and are) supposed to get <i>a number</i> of real, playable settings with the sample courts in every location and in the make-your-own example anyway. The Seasonal Courts existing as a major example model is fine, but putting them right at the start of the book, with the way these things have tended to be structured, I fear that the impression the book will initially give is of conforming to them when they're not supposed to be exhaustive or even <i>that </i>central. Obviously this isn't actually the case even with the 'standard' factions in Vampire, nevermind for Changeling 2e.<br /> <br /> I'm probably just being picky and or demanding at this point. I don't presume to tell anyone, much less writers/developers I am certain will come out with a good product anyways, how to do their job. It is not unreasonable to present a standard setup you could throw anywhere, but until now it seemed like a choice to avoid in the construction of the book.<br /> <br /> I thought it was as the above posters were describing, and it seemed fine that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-04-2017, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:22:10-07:00","id":1073447,"title":"","content":"Even in the Toronto setting it was made clear that the Seasonal Courts and Seelie Courts are very common, to the point that even by absorbing them into itself in the form of the Silver Court, the Seasonal and Seelie Courts could never be ended completely, they're too common else where, they they just regrow eventually. <br /> <br /> The Elizabethean London Freehold from Dark Eras is an example of what we can expect from the other setting court systems according to Rose, so I can live with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:24:47-07:00","id":1073450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073441#post1073441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear that the impression the book will initially give is of conforming to them when they're not supposed to be exhaustive or even <i>that </i>central. </div> </div> </div> </div>It would be helpful to get a sidebar that discusses common systems across the world. The Seasonals are probably a pretty Anglo-/Euro- centric freehold style, exported across the world with Imperialism in general. While Scheherazade's 1001 Nights could be a pretty common style of freehold in many parts of the Middle East. Are the Rose Courts of Dark Eras London still ruling? Did their system spread? Modernize? The Seelie Courts are mentioned in DE and Toronto, let's see them! Where is their primary territory these days? Directionals rule China, has that spread to most of Asia with Honshu and a few others as hold outs? What kind of system reigns in Africa?<br /> <br /> In discussing a global perspective, he often do we see small one-shot Freeholds pop up? Any notable ones that have survived more than a few years or spread beyond a single city?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:29:02-07:00","id":1073454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073441#post1073441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, we were (and are) supposed to get <i>a number</i> of real, playable settings with the sample courts in every location and in the make-your-own example anyway. The Seasonal Courts existing as a major example model is fine, but putting them right at the start of the book, with the way these things have tended to be structured, I fear that the impression the book will initially give is of conforming to them when they're not supposed to be exhaustive or even <i>that </i>central. Obviously this isn't actually the case even with the 'standard' factions in Vampire, nevermind for Changeling 2e.<br /> <br /> I'm probably just being picky and or demanding at this point. I don't presume to tell anyone, much less writers/developers I am certain will come out with a good product anyways, how to do their job. It is not unreasonable to present a standard setup you could throw anywhere, but until now it seemed like a choice to avoid in the construction of the book.<br /> <br /> I thought it was as the above posters were describing, and it seemed fine that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am guessing the Seasonal Courts would still have been in the beginning of the book in David's version as well. I could be wrong about that, but I definitely remember David saying they would be in the book as examples, and I had always assumed the structure would follow the pattern of previous 2e lines.<br /> <br /> I'm just hoping the Freehold Creation rules don't get axed. We haven't seen anything that really suggests they would be, but you know. Stressful uncertainty and all. I don't think I'm alone in feeling that, more than any new material they might preview, what I would appreciate most in an open development blog right now is a rundown of what, from the material that has already been previewed, we can expect to see change significantly, what we can expect to see only minor changes to, and what, if anything, we should not expect to see return at all. I've been getting hyped for a particular vision of CtL2e for a very long time now, so if that vision is going to be changing, I really need to know so I can mentally prepare myself to start getting hyped for the new vision. Just seeing things that are different without knowing what I can or can't count on staying the same is just very, very jarring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-04-2017, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:59:19-07:00","id":1073471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073454#post1073454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am guessing the Seasonal Courts would still have been in the beginning of the book in David's version as well. I could be wrong about that, but I definitely remember David saying they would be in the book as examples, and I had always assumed the structure would follow the pattern of previous 2e lines.<br /> <br /> I'm just hoping the Freehold Creation rules don't get axed. We haven't seen anything that really suggests they would be, but you know. Stressful uncertainty and all. I don't think I'm alone in feeling that, more than any new material they might preview, what I would appreciate most in an open development blog right now is a rundown of what, from the material that has already been previewed, we can expect to see change significantly, what we can expect to see only minor changes to, and what, if anything, we should not expect to see return at all. I've been getting hyped for a particular vision of CtL2e for a very long time now, so if that vision is going to be changing, I really need to know so I can mentally prepare myself to start getting hyped for the new vision. Just seeing things that are different without knowing what I can or can't count on staying the same is just very, very jarring.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seasonal were in Chapter Six, like any of the other Freeholds. Chapter 1 was all Kiths and Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-04-2017, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T18:12:40-07:00","id":1073475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073450#post1073450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be helpful to get a sidebar that discusses common systems across the world. The Seasonals are probably a pretty Anglo-/Euro- centric freehold style, exported across the world with Imperialism in general. While Scheherazade's 1001 Nights could be a pretty common style of freehold in many parts of the Middle East. Are the Rose Courts of Dark Eras London still ruling? Did their system spread? Modernize? The Seelie Courts are mentioned in DE and Toronto, let's see them! Where is their primary territory these days? Directionals rule China, has that spread to most of Asia with Honshu and a few others as hold outs? What kind of system reigns in Africa?<br /> <br /> In discussing a global perspective, he often do we see small one-shot Freeholds pop up? Any notable ones that have survived more than a few years or spread beyond a single city?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be behind this idea, albeit in more fractured form. Having one style be the standard for a continent works for Europe, but even then its a stretch. Having the seasonal courts be Anglo-centric makes sense, but saying that there is an &quot;Asian archetypical court&quot; or &quot;African archetypical court&quot; is almost as much of a turn off as having a worldwide archetype, and is about as probable. African cultures, let alone countries, that are right next to each other are incredibly different! Likewise with China's 19 ethnic groups with populations greater than 1,000,000 people (to say nothing of the dozens with smaller populations). Let their court systems be as diverse!<br /> <br /> But yes, I really would like to see a sidebar about worldwide variance in courts in Chapter 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T18:40:57-07:00","id":1073488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073475#post1073475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd be behind this idea, albeit in more fractured form. Having one style be the standard for a continent works for Europe, but even then its a stretch. Having the seasonal courts be Anglo-centric makes sense, but saying that there is an &quot;Asian archetypical court&quot; or &quot;African archetypical court&quot; is almost as much of a turn off as having a worldwide archetype, and is about as probable. African cultures, let alone countries, that are right next to each other are incredibly different! Likewise with China's 19 ethnic groups with populations greater than 1,000,000 people (to say nothing of the dozens with smaller populations). Let their court systems be as diverse!<br /> <br /> But yes, I really would like to see a sidebar about worldwide variance in courts in Chapter 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me tell you this as someone who's trying to tangle with this specific beast in this very moment: the amount of fairy tales in Africa is <i>staggering</i>. And I'm limiting myself to tales which include beings that fall under the vague terms of what a fairy is. Too much stuff for me to even consider a thing like an &quot;African archetypical court&quot; a possibilty. So many tales with so many differences. Depending on where you look, even having country-wide courts seems like a stretch. Asia is no different.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it in another way, the chapter with examples of Courts from all around the world will be really important, perhaps even more than its correspectives from other gamelines (where I think such chapters already tend to be brilliant)<br /> <br /> That said, I do like the idea of having the Seasonal Courts back as some sort of signature courts. They're iconic and easy to get, acting as an excellent starting point from which a discussion about Courts worldwide can start almost effortlessly. To go to the realm of personal opinions, I do feel like something similar was needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-05-2017, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:24:11-07:00","id":1073503,"title":"","content":"Overall I find this update worrisome. (Not the text itself mind you, the write-up is fine.) It essentially confirms that foundational changes can and will occur to the text of the corebook.<br /> <br /> I had kind of inferred that seasonal courts and maybe the unseelie would be somewhat &quot;elevated&quot; as courts not locked in a particular locale. I have no problems with this, but I've become somewhat emotionally invested in Build-A-Courts, and it won't take a whole lot of backtracking for the concept to lose any weight in practice. If the Seasonals exceed the boundaries of the Court Creation rules, or if fitting the Seasonals requires Court Creation to be so vague as to be guidelines, than the idea of &quot;Different Freeholds have Different Court Systems&quot; will cease to be meaningful or significant, even with concrete examples of that being the case. <br /> <br /> In vampire, for example, clans and covenants outside their respective big five are a definitely a &quot;thing,&quot; but one shouldn't really expect to see any of them unless you've got an ST who is into homebrew. Even the canonical examples of this concept we do have, (the Jiang Shi and Dark Eras Covenants) are notably less robust than their vanilla counterparts. The option for custom clan/covenants is technically there, but the level of effort required to integrate them into an individual game is essentially no different than 1st ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:29:04-07:00","id":1073506,"title":"","content":"I figure courts like the Seasonal, Seelie, Directional Courts and a few others are like major world religions as the most successful court systems spread throughout the world. <br /> <br /> And some are more like massive regional religions, that have a lot of appeal in particular regions where they thrive, but don't spread globally, like the Moon Princess and the 1001 nights Court Systems (although I could see 1001 nights spreading thanks to growing global multiculturalism) .<br /> <br /> So some are just minor local to the region because they serve a particular interest, but are not large at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:37:52-07:00","id":1073509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073503#post1073503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall I find this update worrisome. (Not the text itself mind you, the write-up is fine.) It essentially confirms that foundational changes can and will occur to the text of the corebook.<br /> <br /> I had kind of inferred that seasonal courts and maybe the unseelie would be somewhat &amp;quot;elevated&amp;quot; as courts not locked in a particular locale. I have no problems with this, but I've become somewhat emotionally invested in Build-A-Courts, and it won't take a whole lot of backtracking for the concept to lose any weight in practice. If the Seasonals exceed the boundaries of the Court Creation rules, or if fitting the Seasonals requires Court Creation to be so vague as to be guidelines, than the idea of &amp;quot;Different Freeholds have Different Court Systems&amp;quot; will cease to be meaningful or significant, even with concrete examples of that being the case. <br /> <br /> In vampire, for example, clans and covenants outside their respective big five are a definitely a &amp;quot;thing,&amp;quot; but one shouldn't really expect to see any of them unless you've got an ST who is into homebrew. Even the canonical examples of this concept we do have, (the Jiang Shi and Dark Eras Covenants) are notably less robust than their vanilla counterparts. The option for custom clan/covenants is technically there, but the level of effort required to integrate them into an individual game is essentially no different than 1st ed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Custom clans are easy, Bane/discipline list/thematic quirk, I mean even kiths have more mechanical complexity the Clans. <br /> <br /> Example a clan based on flesh eating movie mutants. <br /> <br /> Bane: Can only embrace those who are closely related to them, Disciplines: Nightmare, Protean, Animalism (Protean takes over the as a physical displine for the Hill Mutant Clan of Vampires for the purpose of Ghouls). <br /> <br /> Done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:40:15-07:00","id":1073510,"title":"","content":"Redacted, I bunged up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:40:41-07:00","id":1073511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073503#post1073503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall I find this update worrisome. (Not the text itself mind you, the write-up is fine.) It essentially confirms that foundational changes can and will occur to the text of the corebook.<br /> <br /> I had kind of inferred that seasonal courts and maybe the unseelie would be somewhat &quot;elevated&quot; as courts not locked in a particular locale. I have no problems with this, but I've become somewhat emotionally invested in Build-A-Courts, and it won't take a whole lot of backtracking for the concept to lose any weight in practice. If the Seasonals exceed the boundaries of the Court Creation rules, or if fitting the Seasonals requires Court Creation to be so vague as to be guidelines, than the idea of &quot;Different Freeholds have Different Court Systems&quot; will cease to be meaningful or significant, even with concrete examples of that being the case. <br /> <br /> In vampire, for example, clans and covenants outside their respective big five are a definitely a &quot;thing,&quot; but one shouldn't really expect to see any of them unless you've got an ST who is into homebrew. Even the canonical examples of this concept we do have, (the Jiang Shi and Dark Eras Covenants) are notably less robust than their vanilla counterparts. The option for custom clan/covenants is technically there, but the level of effort required to integrate them into an individual game is essentially no different than 1st ed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Rose gave an example of the London Courts from Dark Eras as an example of what to expect for the other Settings, so just take a look at that if you have the book and it will be shown as fine.<br /> <br /> I think that Approaches have been replaced by Give and Takes of Bargains, but otherwise courts like haven't changed that much. <br /> <br /> All it is is that the Seasonal Courts get more of a fluff detailing in Chapter 1 (hopefully we didn't lost a bunch of Kiths for this, but I understand).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-04-2017, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:03:52-07:00","id":1073519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073294#post1073294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each setting (not all of the settings are strictly regional) has its own factions, and there's stuff to build your own. But we also present an exciting and accessible group of Courts in 1e-level detail, and those are the seasons.<br /> <br /> Starting with Vampire, there's been a pattern in 2e of encouraging factions unique to each setting while also presenting a set that are flavorful and easy to use in many settings, and Changeling follows that. As in other games, not all factions follow a single metaphysical model -- the French Market's Courts of exchange have some things in common with the seasons, but Hong Kong's factions are set up in an entirely different way. You'll find that the local Courts or other factions are closely tied in to the history of contact and conflict with faerie beings and phenomena in that particular area.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yes, Elizabethan London's Courts are a great example of 2e-style Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm definitely still interested. I just am a tad disappointed that it seems like &quot;build your local system&quot; being a normal part of collective character creation sounds like it's no longer a thing. Over the last year + that had been pretty successfully sold to us following the project as in theme with the &quot;seizing the narrative for yourself&quot; central theme.<br /> <br /> Ironically I was originally disappointed and resistant to losing the central focus on the Seasonal Courts, but that last thematic point had really sold me on David's model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:04:24-07:00","id":1073520,"title":"","content":"I know and understand the company position, but I can see a need to alleviate fears as well, so I will just try to ask a question that could be addressed, and maybe that will set the example.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> So, some stuff was shared and there was some work left to do. Then a new team comes along to finish the job. I believe I remember even some elements needing to be dropped because writers couldn't be found (China?). From what has been shared there was work left and space left, would you say Changeling development is on track with other books in that regard at this point? Is there a major space crunch or is it looking to be an easy fit? I'm still not seeing drastic changes, but I do believe there is a legitimate concern that sections might be dropped as the final leg of this journey was not described clearly. Every time I see something new I wonder &quot;was there space for that?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:07:20-07:00","id":1073521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073511#post1073511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that Approaches have been replaced by Give and Takes of Bargains, but otherwise courts like haven't changed that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure those terms are universal. &quot;Bargaining&quot; is the Autumn Court's niche in the &quot;stages of grief&quot; model of the Courts (Spring is Denial, Summer is Anger, Winter is Depressiom, and &quot;acceptance&quot; is the holy grail everyone is striving for in their own way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:10:17-07:00","id":1073524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073509#post1073509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Custom clans are easy, Bane/discipline list/thematic quirk, I mean even kiths have more mechanical complexity the Clans.<br /> <br /> Example a clan based on flesh eating movie mutants.<br /> <br /> Bane: Can only embrace those who are closely related to them, Disciplines: Nightmare, Protean, Animalism (Protean takes over the as a physical displine for the Hill Mutant Clan of Vampires for the purpose of Ghouls).<br /> <br /> Done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well its kind of over-simplification. Using your example for example: A weakness based around embracing isn't nearly as likely to impact story as automatic Bane gain, or having issues with feeding on the same person more than once. On top of that, compare the Jiang-Shi have a discrete bane AND an embrace restriction. Having no unique discipline, but two uncommon disciplines is also potentially problematic. In short, if someone came to me and said &quot;Want to play Requiem?&quot; and I presented this the answered would probably be &quot;no&quot; or &quot;just play a gangrel and pay extra for nightmare.&quot; I could possibly find a storyteller whose more amicable to this sort of thing, or I could sit down and work out a better balanced Bane-Discipline, that represents going above and beyond the game of Requiem as presented in its current ruleset, and the ST still could have every reason to say no.<br /> <br /> This is less a matter of what can be done, and what will be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:12:53-07:00","id":1073526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073511#post1073511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Approaches have been replaced by Give and Takes of Bargains, but otherwise courts like haven't changed that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, other than the central defining feature of the Y-splat being replaced they haven't changed that much? That's reassuring. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:20:23-07:00","id":1073532,"title":"","content":"The power creation rules that were in earlier drafts are still in the book -- those are the Mantles, as mentioned in the blog post. Some specific mechanics have changed; for example, a +1 bonus to a +2, or a Defense modifier added or removed. If you want Court-specific Contracts for your new Courts, then you'll want to design those yourself -- but that was the case in earlier drafts, as well. (And I think the updated Contract structure is actually going to make that easier than in 1e or earlier drafts, but that's a bit of a tangent.)<br /> <br /> As for a sort of geopolitical look at changeling culture, that'd be an interesting thing for another book -- perhaps a stretch goal along the lines of <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i>. But the models for local Courts are going to be very individual, along the lines of &quot;to the changelings of Reykjavik, seasons have intricate meanings unlike anywhere else in the world,&quot; rather than international, like &quot;Northern Europe has long been under the sorrowful tyranny of the Winter Court.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:26:32-07:00","id":1073533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073532#post1073532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power creation rules that were in earlier drafts are still in the book -- those are the Mantles, as mentioned in the blog post. Some specific mechanics have changed; for example, a +1 bonus to a +2, or a Defense modifier added or removed. If you want Court-specific Contracts for your new Courts, then you'll want to design those yourself -- but that was the case in earlier drafts, as well. (And I think the updated Contract structure is actually going to make that easier than in 1e or earlier drafts, but that's a bit of a tangent.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that <i>is</i> very reassuring, thank you. So would I be correct in assuming based on your phrasing that the power/mantle creation rules are still present but the Freehold creation rules are not? Personal Approaches, but not Bulwarks?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073532#post1073532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a sort of geopolitical look at changeling culture, that'd be an interesting thing for another book -- perhaps a stretch goal along the lines of <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i>. But the models for local Courts are going to be very individual, along the lines of &amp;quot;to the changelings of Reykjavik, seasons have intricate meanings unlike anywhere else in the world,&amp;quot; rather than international, like &amp;quot;Northern Europe has long been under the sorrowful tyranny of the Winter Court.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T21:37:31-07:00","id":1073560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073521#post1073521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure those terms are universal. &amp;quot;Bargaining&amp;quot; is the Autumn Court's niche in the &amp;quot;stages of grief&amp;quot; model of the Courts (Spring is Denial, Summer is Anger, Winter is Depressiom, and &amp;quot;acceptance&amp;quot; is the holy grail everyone is striving for in their own way).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the original Seasonal Courts ever intended to match up with the Stages of Grief. But Changeling 1e was all over the metaphor changelings as abuse victims, and so assigning the Stages to the Courts seemed so perfect to many people. <br /> <br /> In fact, was there ever confirmation or denial that the 1e Seasonals were intended to be metaphors for the Stages? Anybody know? Because I look very askance at reducing complexities into features, and at the idea that your court membership fixes you into a certain Stage without progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T21:41:51-07:00","id":1073561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073560#post1073560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the original Seasonal Courts ever intended to match up with the Stages of Grief. But Changeling 1e was all over the metaphor changelings as abuse victims, and so assigning the Stages to the Courts seemed so perfect to many people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely think it was intentional. Winter and Summer are obvious with their associated emotions. Spring is all about embracing a new life to turn their back on the old and what happened (so denial fits perfectly), and Autumn are steeped in seeking power in the setting's magic system which is all about Pledges &amp; Contracts (i.e. Bargaining).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T21:46:54-07:00","id":1073564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073561#post1073561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I absolutely think it was intentional. Winter and Summer are obvious with their associated emotions. Spring is all about embracing a new life to turn their back on the old and what happened (so denial fits perfectly), and Autumn are steeped in seeking power in the setting's magic system which is all about Pledges &amp; Contracts (i.e. Bargaining).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like I said, the Seasonals and the Stages resonate very strongly. But I'm still miffed about what it implies to individual members of the Courts. Like, a Spring Courtier only experiences denial in regards to her Durance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T21:47:08-07:00","id":1073565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073533#post1073533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that <i>is</i> very reassuring, thank you. So would I be correct in assuming based on your phrasing that the power/mantle creation rules are still present but the Freehold creation rules are not? Personal Approaches, but not Bulwarks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting creation is built around chronicle themes, local supernatural phenomena, and mapping relationships for the player characters, rather than a freehold template. It's really neat: for example, you can generate a theme of Truth and Lies and then give that theme &quot;face&quot; characters and supernatural props, then tie those to the players' motley.<br /> <br /> To be really direct: there's nothing from the early drafts that's no longer allowed -- if you want to hold the Gentry at bay by forcing them into a story, that's valid. But Courts aren't all built on a single style of magical defense.<br /> <br /> A Court is a group of changelings that has its own methods for a) helping changelings own their own lives, b) building and maintaining local community, and c) avoiding, holding back, or misdirecting the Gentry. They work and they party and they scrap and they love. Your Court are your people, and when the Huntsman has chased you down and your back's against the wall, your Court opens the secret door or jumps him from behind or knocks down every brick of that wall and fucking buries him under it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-05-2017, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T22:00:10-07:00","id":1073571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073561#post1073561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely think it was intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicit confirmation that it wasn't <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?567853-NWOD-The-NWOD-as-a-reaction-to-itself&amp;p=13699141#post13699141\" target=\"_blank\">exists</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T22:16:30-07:00","id":1073574,"title":"","content":"Would it be too much right now to ask for another example of how Courts work, using the new terms this time so that we can piece out what's the difference from previous previews?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073571#post1073571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explicit confirmation that it wasn't <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?567853-NWOD-The-NWOD-as-a-reaction-to-itself&amp;p=13699141#post13699141\" target=\"_blank\">exists</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's one worry off my back about Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T22:28:13-07:00","id":1073578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073565#post1073565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting creation is built around chronicle themes, local supernatural phenomena, and mapping relationships for the player characters, rather than a freehold template. It's really neat: for example, you can generate a theme of Truth and Lies and then give that theme &amp;quot;face&amp;quot; characters and supernatural props, then tie those to the players' motley.<br /> <br /> To be really direct: there's nothing from the early drafts that's no longer allowed -- if you want to hold the Gentry at bay by forcing them into a story, that's valid. But Courts aren't all built on a single style of magical defense.<br /> <br /> A Court is a group of changelings that has its own methods for a) helping changelings own their own lives, b) building and maintaining local community, and c) avoiding, holding back, or misdirecting the Gentry. They work and they party and they scrap and they love. Your Court are your people, and when the Huntsman has chased you down and your back's against the wall, your Court opens the secret door or jumps him from behind or knocks down every brick of that wall and fucking buries him under it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thank you. I really enjoyed the concept of Bulwarks, but knowing this I'm excited to see what you've done with Freehold creation in their place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T23:17:30-07:00","id":1073594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073565#post1073565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting creation is built around chronicle themes, local supernatural phenomena, and mapping relationships for the player characters, rather than a freehold template. It's really neat: for example, you can generate a theme of Truth and Lies and then give that theme &quot;face&quot; characters and supernatural props, then tie those to the players' motley.<br /> <br /> To be really direct: there's nothing from the early drafts that's no longer allowed -- if you want to hold the Gentry at bay by forcing them into a story, that's valid. But Courts aren't all built on a single style of magical defense.<br /> <br /> A Court is a group of changelings that has its own methods for a) helping changelings own their own lives, b) building and maintaining local community, and c) avoiding, holding back, or misdirecting the Gentry. They work and they party and they scrap and they love. Your Court are your people, and when the Huntsman has chased you down and your back's against the wall, your Court opens the secret door or jumps him from behind or knocks down every brick of that wall and fucking buries him under it.</div> </div> </div> </div>...surprisingly, this doesn't change a great deal about the freehold I was crafting on and off again. While it sadly removes the aspect where every court needs to produce a successful, historical play per year, most of the groundwork I had for the courts is still valid. History and Perceptions Therein is still a pretty strong theme for it...this has given me much to think about.<br /> <br /> That said, I like the idea of bulwarks enough I might just work it in somehow. Vaults that require a certain role to be played by their owners in order to access the contents, while brute forcing it physically or magically just produces a dusty room (or worse). Actually, that works rather well for the Dust Court, given they tend to hoard things for the freehold...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T23:58:26-07:00","id":1073599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073565#post1073565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting creation is built around chronicle themes, local supernatural phenomena, and mapping relationships for the player characters, rather than a freehold template. It's really neat: for example, you can generate a theme of Truth and Lies and then give that theme &quot;face&quot; characters and supernatural props, then tie those to the players' motley.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that work for using a setting for more than one game, or making the setting before you make the player characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T04:41:44-07:00","id":1073669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073532#post1073532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power creation rules that were in earlier drafts are still in the book -- those are the Mantles, as mentioned in the blog post. Some specific mechanics have changed; for example, a +1 bonus to a +2, or a Defense modifier added or removed. If you want Court-specific Contracts for your new Courts, then you'll want to design those yourself -- but that was the case in earlier drafts, as well. (And I think the updated Contract structure is actually going to make that easier than in 1e or earlier drafts, but that's a bit of a tangent.)<br /> <br /> As for a sort of geopolitical look at changeling culture, that'd be an interesting thing for another book -- perhaps a stretch goal along the lines of <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i>. But the models for local Courts are going to be very individual, along the lines of &amp;quot;to the changelings of Reykjavik, seasons have intricate meanings unlike anywhere else in the world,&amp;quot; rather than international, like &amp;quot;Northern Europe has long been under the sorrowful tyranny of the Winter Court.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Very interesting. So Mantles are still in, with some changes, although the basic structure is the same. <br /> <br /> Assuming Toronto is still in, I wonder what Supernatural Phenomena will be for the setting Angels? Djinn? A Pheomena that causes escaping Changelings from across the world to find themselves in Toronto instead of their country of origin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:21:20-07:00","id":1073758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073565#post1073565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting creation is built around chronicle themes, local supernatural phenomena, and mapping relationships for the player characters, rather than a freehold template. It's really neat: for example, you can generate a theme of Truth and Lies and then give that theme &quot;face&quot; characters and supernatural props, then tie those to the players' motley.<br /> <br /> To be really direct: there's nothing from the early drafts that's no longer allowed -- if you want to hold the Gentry at bay by forcing them into a story, that's valid. But Courts aren't all built on a single style of magical defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying stuff from the early drafts is still 'allowed' is a little disingenuous I think. It's not like you as writers can force anyone to do anything once we have the book in hand. If something isn't supported, then it's not going to be used. If this new version of court creation isn't viable, it's not going to be used. If setting creation is just jotting down a few themes and supernatural mysteries to explore then everyone's going to be shoehorned into the Seasonal courts again and you might as well skip customized freeholds entirely. 1ed had some really cool alternate court ideas but no one ever used them because they weren't supported. It's like the Mage book saying there are Nameless Orders all around but unless you get someone that really likes homebrew stuff, it's never going to be played because there is a ton of information, merits, and other mechanics that support the regular orders. If alternate styles of freeholds are going to work, there needs to be a real way to create them included in the book, and the Seasonals need to follow those rules. Simply mapping character relationships and everything seems very vague and fluffy. Obviously we haven't seen it yet and I hope it rocks because I really want Changeling 2ed to succeed, but I don't think what we've already seen of court creation should be just thrown out with the bath water. Changed if you don't like Bulwarks and Approaches, but give us some crunch here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:43:32-07:00","id":1073772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073564#post1073564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, like I said, the Seasonals and the Stages resonate very strongly. But I'm still miffed about what it implies to individual members of the Courts. Like, a Spring Courtier only experiences denial in regards to her Durance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Satchel already pointed out that this isn't intended to be explicitly the case but something that you might also want to consider is that this is not a monolithic lens. Even if, for example, the Five Stages of Grief are considered universal (a shaky assumption but let's run with it), there is a plurality of ways in which people deal with that. Someone in denial might seek out extreme treatments for a fatal illness, despite the likelihood of their survival being nil; or they might find religion and hold out for a miracle, or use a belief in an afterlife as justification to not have to deal with the immediate (which isn't to say that a belief in an afterlife is wrong; just that you need to deal with that your death is coming and that you will have to think and plan about what that means); or they might, as is the stereotype, simply pretend nothing's wrong at all and go about their day as if nothing has changed.<br /> <br /> Denial doesn't mean just going &quot;It didn't happen&quot;. It means a refusal to confront and accept that something has <i>changed</i>. The Spring Court's dances with desire come from a place that wants to prove that Arcadia didn't change them, or that they're still masters of their own destiny; that they still have <i>control</i> of their own lives.<br /> <br /> This can manifest in a plethora of ways. The stereotypical bon vivant who surrounds themselves in pleasure is only one example of someone who refuses to accept things have changed, indulging in mindless enjoyment so they don't have to think about how the danger is still out there or so they can drown out the memories of the pains (and <i>pleasures</i>) of Arcadia. Like a person with chronic depression, surrounding themselves with other people can silence the pain, for a while at least.<br /> <br /> But it can also be the artist who wants to create one grand masterpiece; something truly immortal and on par with the Mona Lisa, or the Venus de Milo, or Handel's Messiah. They want to create the next grand novel or the next great painting or <i>something</i>, because they want to create something that will outlast them; all based on the secret feeling that it makes them invulnerable. If their music reaches all the ears of the world, it doesn't matter if their body dies; some part of their soul lives on forever in the hearts and minds of everyone.<br /> <br /> Or it could be the sorcerer who is delving deeply into forbidden knowledge in ways to rival even the Autumn Court; gathering secrets and bargains like an armory of blades. If they can hone their desire to a razor's edge, they can create a blade which can cut through any thorn vine or spider-silk armour. And, plus... Maybe you have something they want.<br /> <br /> You see my point. Denial doesn't have to be conscious or obvious; it just means that you're not coming to accept reality. Rather than face the pain, you drown it out with pleasure; rather than accept the danger, you try to make yourself unassailable. You sacrifice your life to the cause; turning away serious relationships that might draw you out of the non-stop party or away from your great work; you make everyone an enemy when they're no longer useful to you, because what isn't useful is a threat.<br /> <br /> So. Yeah. Maybe that doesn't change your perspective but, just in case, there it is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:28:57-07:00","id":1073788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073565#post1073565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting creation is built around chronicle themes, local supernatural phenomena, and mapping relationships for the player characters, rather than a freehold template. It's really neat: for example, you can generate a theme of Truth and Lies and then give that theme &quot;face&quot; characters and supernatural props, then tie those to the players' motley.<br /> <br /> To be really direct: there's nothing from the early drafts that's no longer allowed -- if you want to hold the Gentry at bay by forcing them into a story, that's valid. But Courts aren't all built on a single style of magical defense.<br /> <br /> A Court is a group of changelings that has its own methods for a) helping changelings own their own lives, b) building and maintaining local community, and c) avoiding, holding back, or misdirecting the Gentry. They work and they party and they scrap and they love. Your Court are your people, and when the Huntsman has chased you down and your back's against the wall, your Court opens the secret door or jumps him from behind or knocks down every brick of that wall and fucking buries him under it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you planning any big changes on the gentry themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:35:49-07:00","id":1073793,"title":"","content":"EDIT: answered above","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-05-2017, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T12:52:48-07:00","id":1073839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073758#post1073758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying stuff from the early drafts is still 'allowed' is a little disingenuous I think. It's not like you as writers can force anyone to do anything once we have the book in hand. If something isn't supported, then it's not going to be used. If this new version of court creation isn't viable, it's not going to be used. If setting creation is just jotting down a few themes and supernatural mysteries to explore then everyone's going to be shoehorned into the Seasonal courts again and you might as well skip customized freeholds entirely. 1ed had some really cool alternate court ideas but no one ever used them because they weren't supported. It's like the Mage book saying there are Nameless Orders all around but unless you get someone that really likes homebrew stuff, it's never going to be played because there is a ton of information, merits, and other mechanics that support the regular orders. If alternate styles of freeholds are going to work, there needs to be a real way to create them included in the book, and the Seasonals need to follow those rules. Simply mapping character relationships and everything seems very vague and fluffy. Obviously we haven't seen it yet and I hope it rocks because I really want Changeling 2ed to succeed, but I don't think what we've already seen of court creation should be just thrown out with the bath water. Changed if you don't like Bulwarks and Approaches, but give us some crunch here!</div> </div> </div> </div> I think at least the premade settings will have support, I mean Honshu and Toronto are already very playable and I doubt that will change that much in the new versions. At least I hope not as I really loved both those settings and they deserve to be retained even if a few things change in them. So while the other courts in the book might not be as detailed as the Seasonal Courts, they will likely be fully functional and usable, like they are in the playtest, if a bit different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T13:26:52-07:00","id":1073858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073839#post1073839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think at least the premade settings will have support, I mean Honshu and Toronto are already very playable and I doubt that will change that much in the new versions. At least I hope not as I really loved both those settings and they deserve to be retained even if a few things change in them. So while the other courts in the book might not be as detailed as the Seasonal Courts, they will likely be fully functional and usable, like they are in the playtest, if a bit different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they going to include the contacts for Toronto that we haven't seen yet though? Or is it going to be relegated to &quot;make it up yourselves&quot; the way ask the 1ed alternate court contracts were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T15:22:49-07:00","id":1073904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073565#post1073565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting creation is built around chronicle themes, local supernatural phenomena, and mapping relationships for the player characters, rather than a freehold template. It's really neat: for example, you can generate a theme of Truth and Lies and then give that theme &quot;face&quot; characters and supernatural props, then tie those to the players' motley.<br /> <br /> To be really direct: there's nothing from the early drafts that's no longer allowed -- if you want to hold the Gentry at bay by forcing them into a story, that's valid. But Courts aren't all built on a single style of magical defense.<br /> <br /> A Court is a group of changelings that has its own methods for a) helping changelings own their own lives, b) building and maintaining local community, and c) avoiding, holding back, or misdirecting the Gentry. They work and they party and they scrap and they love. Your Court are your people, and when the Huntsman has chased you down and your back's against the wall, your Court opens the secret door or jumps him from behind or knocks down every brick of that wall and fucking buries him under it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say I really appreciate the way you put this. It sounds like setting creation has a greater breadth of factors that can influence or shape a freehold's defenses, while allowing the same kind of story-based protection as in the original previews. My doubts are for the moment quelled, and I'm very curious about other examples.<br /> <br /> Your short list of what a Court means to Changelings also makes for a compelling description, looking forward to seeing it explored through all the courts in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T18:51:53-07:00","id":1073969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073858#post1073858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are they going to include the contacts for Toronto that we haven't seen yet though? Or is it going to be relegated to &amp;quot;make it up yourselves&amp;quot; the way ask the 1ed alternate court contracts were?</div> </div> </div> </div> 2e contracts don't take anywhere near the space of 1e contracts, so I think there is a reasonable chance that they kept the contracts for Toronto and Honshu, but that is my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T09:00:51-07:00","id":1074169,"title":"","content":"So, just to be sure. Changeling will or will not have a special sorcery power?<br /> I devoured the preview but didn't see anything that points towards this. T-T<br /> Please tell me I'm wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T11:05:15-07:00","id":1074236,"title":"","content":"*Readz the rough draft*<br /> <br /> This stuff is AMAZING!! More! xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T17:32:39-07:00","id":1074421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073565#post1073565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be really direct: there's nothing from the early drafts that's no longer allowed -- if you want to hold the Gentry at bay by forcing them into a story, that's valid. But Courts aren't all built on a single style of magical defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... actually makes a lot of sense. <br /> <br /> To go back to the idea of a Hogwarts Freehold that I made when Court Creation was first previewed: under this new scheme, Gryffindor's kind of like Summer, taking any threats head-on, marching to fight the Gentry with cold iron in hand; Ravenclaw is kind of like Autumn, digging up old Contracts and obscure arcane stuff to ward the Gentry off; Slytherin either tries to appease the Gentry to buy the Freehold enough time to prepare, or seems to run away before showing up with backup at a critical point in the fight; Hufflepuff does whatever is needed at the time- supply runs, medic duty, rear guard, plugging a hole in the lines- without complaint or expectation of thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T02:49:07-07:00","id":1074567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074169#post1074169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just to be sure. Changeling will or will not have a special sorcery power?</div> </div> </div> </div> Define special sorcery power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T07:03:44-07:00","id":1074639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074567#post1074567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Define special sorcery power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire - Cru\u00e1c, Theban Sorcery<br /> Werewolf - Rites","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T07:57:12-07:00","id":1074654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074639#post1074639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire - Cru\u00e1c, Theban Sorcery<br /> Werewolf - Rites</div> </div> </div> </div> So... what exactly do you want from these? Extended actions that take longer than Instant action combat abilities? Separate powers? Flexable abilties on the cheap? Exclusivity? Something clearly labeled?<br /> <br /> I'm honestly curious here. What do you feel this ability would be like? And how would it be different from, say, Goblin Vows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-07-2017, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T09:14:18-07:00","id":1074689,"title":"","content":"I'd say Hedge Shaping or Goblin Vows would be closest to &quot;Sorcery&quot; .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T11:50:01-07:00","id":1074770,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, I'd advise against giving the Autumn Court a specific whole extra power set, and instead focus on working within the established Court construction system. To that end, I'd rather give them bonuses to some specific action(s) or custom merits, and maybe tie it together with their Contracts, rather than just make Cruac 2: Electric Boogaloo.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, perhaps merits or Contracts tied to enhancing their Kenning, so that they can differentiate different types of supernatural phenomena? Or the ability to sort of pre-bargain a Goblin Vow; letting you know what the deal is up-front and do it in advance to get the desired result, rather than doing it out of desperation and risking a nasty curse. Just spitballing, but there's a few thoughts.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even have to be all that much; just enough that, when something supernatural and spooky is going on, everyone looks to the Autumn Courtier first for advice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:08:46-07:00","id":1074785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073560#post1073560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the original Seasonal Courts ever intended to match up with the Stages of Grief. But Changeling 1e was all over the metaphor changelings as abuse victims, and so assigning the Stages to the Courts seemed so perfect to many people.<br /> <br /> In fact, was there ever confirmation or denial that the 1e Seasonals were intended to be metaphors for the Stages? Anybody know? Because I look very askance at reducing complexities into features, and at the idea that your court membership fixes you into a certain Stage without progress.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe in point of fact the developers specifically stated it was never their intention (consciously, mind you) to set it up that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:42:59-07:00","id":1074811,"title":"","content":"And for my part, this write up makes me tentatively more excited for 2e. This FEELS like the game I fell in love with. If all of the Courts are written up this way, with these sections modestly devoted to what they do day to day in the Freehold and while in power, then hells yeah I'm in. I think the homebrew Court creation system is fine for the STs feeling up for it, but I don't have the time or energy and as a player I'd be wary that the ST wouldn't make anything as fun to play as the Seasons or similar systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:54:36-07:00","id":1074826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074770#post1074770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general rule, I'd advise against giving the Autumn Court a specific whole extra power set, and instead focus on working within the established Court construction system. To that end, I'd rather give them bonuses to some specific action(s) or custom merits, and maybe tie it together with their Contracts, rather than just make Cruac 2: Electric Boogaloo.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, perhaps merits or Contracts tied to enhancing their Kenning, so that they can differentiate different types of supernatural phenomena? Or the ability to sort of pre-bargain a Goblin Vow; letting you know what the deal is up-front and do it in advance to get the desired result, rather than doing it out of desperation and risking a nasty curse. Just spitballing, but there's a few thoughts.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even have to be all that much; just enough that, when something supernatural and spooky is going on, everyone looks to the Autumn Courtier first for advice.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could do that very simply with Autumn Mantle and Contract. <br /> <br /> Maybe a Contract that reflects magic back at a caster and a mantle that grants a bonus to the occult skill, Goblin Vows: Sorcery, and a spell book based Token Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:10:04-07:00","id":1074838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074785#post1074785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe in point of fact the developers specifically stated it was never their intention (consciously, mind you) to set it up that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, yeah, they said it wasn't intentionally written that way, but that it was a cool interpretation that worked well within the setting as-written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:42:47-07:00","id":1074855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074838#post1074838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, yeah, they said it wasn't intentionally written that way, but that it was a cool interpretation that worked well within the setting as-written.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a natural connection to make for a species (humans) who see patterns even when none were intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:54:30-07:00","id":1074857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074826#post1074826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do that very simply with Autumn Mantle and Contract.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Contract that reflects magic back at a caster and a mantle that grants a bonus to the occult skill, Goblin Vows: Sorcery, and a spell book based Token Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definitely not do the first one. Countermagic is always a colossal pain in the ass and a terrible idea for a Court-exclusive thing. The others... Eh. Lackluster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T15:16:03-07:00","id":1074875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074857#post1074857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd definitely not do the first one. Countermagic is always a colossal pain in the ass and a terrible idea for a Court-exclusive thing. The others... Eh. Lackluster.</div> </div> </div> </div> It was a hypothetical on the cuff example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T15:20:46-07:00","id":1074878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074855#post1074855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a natural connection to make for a species (humans) who see patterns even when none were intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, you know, human minds are weird in more ways than one. Just because a theme or message was not consciously put into a work by the artist doesn't mean it's not there. It may have been included subconsciously, a product of the artist's biases and preferences, or it may be more of an immergent property of the other, more intentional themes and messages. They're still valid. And I think the Kubler-Ross interpretation of the Seasonal courts is likewise a valid reading of Changeling, even if it wasn't the writers' conscious intention. Though, it's important to take that context into account when applying the Kubler-Ross interpretation to Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T15:53:37-07:00","id":1074892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074857#post1074857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd definitely not do the first one. Countermagic is always a colossal pain in the ass and a terrible idea for a Court-exclusive thing. The others... Eh. Lackluster.</div> </div> </div> </div> You must hate the Contract of Abjuration then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074878#post1074878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, you know, human minds are weird in more ways than one. Just because a theme or message was not consciously put into a work by the artist doesn't mean it's not there. It may have been included subconsciously, a product of the artist's biases and preferences, or it may be more of an immergent property of the other, more intentional themes and messages. They're still valid. And I think the Kubler-Ross interpretation of the Seasonal courts is likewise a valid reading of Changeling, even if it wasn't the writers' conscious intention. Though, it's important to take that context into account when applying the Kubler-Ross interpretation to Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is not to you, Charlaquin, but I feel that it should be mentioned. Implying that the writers were putting in the stages of grief unconciously is kind of .... problematic to me. Not only because it is implying that writes don't actually know what they're writing and intending to convey (and that others know better), but that it misses other possibilities. <br /> <br /> Were you familiar that the writer of Fahrenheit 451 was told, to his face during a lecture he was holding, that his book was about the dangers of government censorship, despite the man himself denying it? There's lots of people who will swear, up and down, that the story is about censorship, all evidence or claims to the contrary. Now, I'm not saying this is what's going on here, but there's enough similarities for me to be bothered by it.<br /> <br /> Inside Out, the movie, tapped into Joy, Sadness, Anger, Disgust and Fear as the five emotions because that's actually a real thing. Science has a very strong leaning that there are five (give or take one) universal emotions that all humans have. Is it any surprise that the Seasonals tap into these major emotions as well as any number of other things, including the Stage of Grief? There is a link between the Seasonal Emotions and the emotions of SoG, but its not necessarily cause-and-effect. There could be any number of reasons. I personally like using the Seasonal Court emotions by linking them to holidays - Halloween, Christmas, Easter and July 4th (US only). Each emotion relates to the themes of each holiday, and nothing more. <br /> <br /> If someone wants to link the four Seasonal emotions to the Stages of Grief, more power to them. If that's the type of thing they enjoy, more power to them. But suggesting that its <i>really</i> what the authors intended, despite any protest? That's very iffy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T16:23:15-07:00","id":1074895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074892#post1074892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not to you, Charlaquin, but I feel that it should be mentioned. Implying that the writers were putting in the stages of grief unconciously is kind of .... problematic to me. Not only because it is implying that writes don't actually know what they're writing and intending to convey (and that others know better), but that it misses other possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... Works always convey messages the artists did not consider or intend. That doesn't mean they don't know what they're doing, nor does it invalidate the conscious and intended meaning. It's just part of the nature of art, and the interpretation thereof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074892#post1074892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were you familiar that the writer of Fahrenheit 451 was told, to his face during a lecture he was holding, that his book was about the dangers of government censorship, despite the man himself denying it? There's lots of people who will swear, up and down, that the story is about censorship, all evidence or claims to the contrary. Now, I'm not saying this is what's going on here, but there's enough similarities for me to be bothered by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death of the author. The Fahrenheit 451 does contain messages about the dangers of government censorship, whether they were intended or not. While the lack of intent to convey those messages is important context to consider when critically analyzing Fahrenheit 451, but it's still a valid way to interpret the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074892#post1074892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inside Out, the movie, tapped into Joy, Sadness, Anger, Disgust and Fear as the five emotions because that's actually a real thing. Science has a very strong leaning that there are five (give or take one) universal emotions that all humans have. Is it any surprise that the Seasonals tap into these major emotions as well as any number of other things, including the Stage of Grief? There is a link between the Seasonal Emotions and the emotions of SoG, but its not necessarily cause-and-effect. There could be any number of reasons. I personally like using the Seasonal Court emotions by linking them to holidays - Halloween, Christmas, Easter and July 4th (US only). Each emotion relates to the themes of each holiday, and nothing more.<br /> <br /> If someone wants to link the four Seasonal emotions to the Stages of Grief, more power to them. If that's the type of thing they enjoy, more power to them. But suggesting that its <i>really</i> what the authors intended, despite any protest? That's very iffy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a big difference between &quot;this is a message that exists in the work despite not being intentionally put there&quot; and &quot;this is what the authors <i>really</i> intended.&quot; Intent implies conscious will anyway, so saying a message was included unconsciously specifically <i>does not</i> mean it's the author's &quot;real&quot; intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T18:05:00-07:00","id":1074929,"title":"","content":"... you know what, I'm gone. Bye all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-07-2017, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T18:07:54-07:00","id":1074930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074895#post1074895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm... Works always convey messages the artists did not consider or intend. That doesn't mean they don't know what they're doing, nor does it invalidate the conscious and intended meaning. It's just part of the nature of art, and the interpretation thereof.<br /> <br /> There is a big difference between &quot;this is a message that exists in the work despite not being intentionally put there&quot; and &quot;this is what the authors <i>really</i> intended.&quot; Intent implies conscious will anyway, so saying a message was included unconsciously specifically <i>does not</i> mean it's the author's &quot;real&quot; intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I've seen too many people insisting that interpreting the Seasonals as the Stages is the One True Way and the Only Right Way that Changeling 1e should be read as. The difference is there, and it's big like you say, but not everyone bothers to (or is able to) spot it.<br /> <br /> Taking the Spring Court for example. Desire has many causes and expressions, of which Denial is part of. Denial, too, has many causes and expressions, of which Desire is part of. The two overlap in a Venn diagram. 1e Spring Court was placed inside or at least overlapping with that middle ground. But which circle should it lean to? My vote goes to Desire, because intense passions in general fit in with almost any story. The Stages of Grief work nicely for, well, grief and dealing with it, but that's a narrower narrative niche than &quot;emotions.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T20:20:40-07:00","id":1074966,"title":"","content":"In case it's at all unclear, I am not trying to suggest that the Kubler-Ross interpretation of the Seasonal Courts is the &quot;correct&quot; interpretation, or that it was the authors' intent. In fact, we have word-of-authors that they never considered that interpretation, though some thought it was cool. I think it's an interesting interpretation, and I do think the stages of grief suit some, but not all, aspects of the Seasonal Courts pretty well. I'm sorry that I phrased it as &quot;subconscious influence&quot; as that seems to have struck some nerves I had no intention of striking. I meant not to imply in any way that the authors were somehow creating the Seasonal Courts specifically to fit within the Kubler-Ross model without their own knowledge. Apparently &quot;subconscious&quot; means something different to me than it does to others? Or maybe I'm just failing spectacularly to express my perspective. Either way, sorry for bringing it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T21:52:02-07:00","id":1074990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074966#post1074966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case it's at all unclear, I am not trying to suggest that the Kubler-Ross interpretation of the Seasonal Courts is the &quot;correct&quot; interpretation, or that it was the authors' intent. In fact, we have word-of-authors that they never considered that interpretation, though some thought it was cool. I think it's an interesting interpretation, and I do think the stages of grief suit some, but not all, aspects of the Seasonal Courts pretty well. I'm sorry that I phrased it as &quot;subconscious influence&quot; as that seems to have struck some nerves I had no intention of striking. I meant not to imply in any way that the authors were somehow creating the Seasonal Courts specifically to fit within the Kubler-Ross model without their own knowledge. Apparently &quot;subconscious&quot; means something different to me than it does to others? Or maybe I'm just failing spectacularly to express my perspective. Either way, sorry for bringing it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't speak for other people, but at least for me saying that Changeling's Seasonal Courts are about the Kubler-Ross model is the equivalent of saying Mage is about Atlantis, or Werewolf is about Spirit Cops, or Demon is about rogue robots. Sure, it's an interpretation of the game that isn't completely baseless, but it became a memetic paraphrase that pretends to summarize the entire game when it's actually a massive reduction of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T22:58:15-07:00","id":1075013,"title":"","content":"I don't... think I ever said the Seasonal Courts were about the Kubler-Ross model. But, I can see it's a soft spot for more experienced Changeling fans, my apologies for addressing the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T08:24:40-07:00","id":1075136,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't care if the authors intended the Grief connection or not, if it occurred to people read it, it's a safe bet some Changelings would make the connection as well. <br /> <br /> Anyways it's not really important, back on topic I'm curious as to how give and take works on courts systems that don't have courts taking turns governing in a cycle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T11:57:00-07:00","id":1075198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075013#post1075013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't... think I ever said the Seasonal Courts were about the Kubler-Ross model. But, I can see it's a soft spot for more experienced Changeling fans, my apologies for addressing the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me the only important part is that the idea is something that CAN be explored by the ST, not something which NEEDS to be explored. Some people, often victims of real life trauma, complained that the Changeling game offered the stages of grief minus actual recovery as their society with the implication that there is no getting over tragedy or turning your life around. People were understandably upset by that idea and became turned off by changeling as a result. So its important to emphasize that Changeling has a lot to offer for a lot of people, and that there's plenty of interesting stories to be told with the Seasons that don't involve poking at people's personal tragedies. Its out there and ready for those who don't balk at the idea, but its by no means THE way to play the game. <br /> <br /> Not that you need that qualification, but still feels important to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:01:24-07:00","id":1075458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075136#post1075136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways it's not really important, back on topic I'm curious as to how give and take works on courts systems that don't have courts taking turns governing in a cycle?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think they'll need to do the whole &quot;share power&quot; thing anymore. While that was a thing in 1e, I'm not really getting that vibe in 2e. We've had &quot;its the stories&quot; with Toronto and Honshu, and now the Seasonals seem to have a lot more focus on their Bargains being the root of their defense rather than sharing power. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:28:13-07:00","id":1075471,"title":"","content":"They really wouldn't have to shift much in how those courts work I guess, just change court approaches and Personal approaches to something that fits the new mechanics.<br /> <br /> And maybe make it more clear what element of the Wyrd was bargained with to create the court (Ivory Court might bargain with Ivory or Mithra, Fire Fat might bargain with Fire Rat or Rebellion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-09-2017, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:41:20-07:00","id":1075475,"title":"","content":"Bulwarks used to define things, but we have no idea whether or not it'll be replaced by anything more than vague guidelines yet since court creation isn't going to be a priority anymore. I hope we see the new creation rules soon, and that they're specific enough to be an actual viable option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T13:16:16-07:00","id":1075565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075475#post1075475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bulwarks used to define things, but we have no idea whether or not it'll be replaced by anything more than vague guidelines yet since court creation isn't going to be a priority anymore. I hope we see the new creation rules soon, and that they're specific enough to be an actual viable option.</div> </div> </div> </div> That could work. <br /> <br /> There are other rules I'm concerned about such as Embracing the Wyrd or Dropping the Mask, does Clarity still work the same way (if I had to guess, I'd guess it does), Hedge Warping, Dreamwalking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:11:07-07:00","id":1075597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075565#post1075565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does Clarity still work the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good lord, I hope so. Clarity in the playtest preview was pitch perfect for Changeling, I will be devistated if it changes significantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:21:42-07:00","id":1075603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075597#post1075597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good lord, I hope so. Clarity in the playtest preview was pitch perfect for Changeling, I will be devistated if it changes significantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main gripe is that I desperately hope Touchstones are better-integrated in the final product, because in the state I last saw them in (which was a long while back) the system was pretty much &quot;it works like it does in Vampire, but the whole edifice is opt-in rather than a baseline aspect of the template and there's no drawback to not having a Touchstone if you never take a Touchstone in the first place.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:33:58-07:00","id":1075607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075603#post1075603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main gripe is that I desperately hope Touchstones are better-integrated in the final product, because in the state I last saw them in (which was a long while back) the system was pretty much &quot;it works like it does in Vampire, but the whole edifice is opt-in rather than a baseline aspect of the template and there's no drawback to not having a Touchstone if you never take a Touchstone in the first place.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with that. If Touchstones could be implemented better without sacrificing the function of Clarity Triggers and the Acuity Condition, that would be a welcome improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-09-2017, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:43:44-07:00","id":1075649,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Touchstones can be tied to Bargains (the type of Pledges previews before, not the Court system previewed now), in the sense of giving the changeling a place to belong in the mortal world, which in turn hides and protects them from the Fae.<br /> <br /> And while typing that, I just realized that Pledge-Bargains and Court-Bargains work on the same principle. The changeling is concealed from Arcadia by doing something for the other party. If this is right, consider me sold on the new Court system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T18:53:49-07:00","id":1075669,"title":"","content":"Touchstones feel like they'd be something really good for Changelings to have. People who have severe anxiety tend to feel calmed by having something stable in their lives. Having it just be &quot;There's this important person in your life who may never actually come up in the game&quot;, though, is bad. It might work in solo play but, in a group game, an ST can only handle so many things at once.<br /> <br /> It'd feel better to chuck Touchstones as people and work them instead in as behaviours; things a Changeling <i>must</i> do because doing so gives them a sense of control and grounding in reality, the breaking of which shatters a sense of security. Anything that encourages the odd, mad behaviours of the Lost is a good thing. Having a merit for something or someone akin to a Touchstone that provides a bonus when they're around might be good too, but I fear such a thing faces the same problem as the standard Touchstone; it won't really <i>be</i> there when the Changeling needs it in most cases.<br /> <br /> If you <i>did</i> want to keep them as is... Maybe a merit that lets a Changeling who suffered a recent Clarity drop a chance to reroll if they seek out their source of stability and comfort as soon as they can? For example, a Beast who was just arrested by the police and who spent their time in jail having a nervous breakdown, screaming and begging to be let out of the cell that reminds them all too much of an Arcadian cage, racing from there to the home of their lover and taking comfort in their arms. Or an Elemental whose mother just passed away wandering to a local park they spent time playing in as a child and sitting there a while; shedding tears of amber and finding, if not comfort, at least a peacefulness. Even give a dice bonus to Clarity rolls if the Changeling has some memento of an object from that person or place, like a wedding ring, or a flower they plucked that morning, or <i>something</i> that could give a potential rival a clue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T19:09:26-07:00","id":1075673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075649#post1075649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Touchstones can be tied to Bargains (the type of Pledges previews before, not the Court system previewed now), in the sense of giving the changeling a place to belong in the mortal world, which in turn hides and protects them from the Fae.<br /> <br /> And while typing that, I just realized that Pledge-Bargains and Court-Bargains work on the same principle. The changeling is concealed from Arcadia by doing something for the other party. If this is right, consider me sold on the new Court system.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T22:28:10-07:00","id":1075735,"title":"","content":"Speaking of systems I hope don't see <i>too</i> drastic of changes, I always thought Bargains looked an awful lot like Touchstone relationships. I wonder if those elements could be worked together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T01:40:59-07:00","id":1075793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075735#post1075735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I always thought Bargains looked an awful lot like Touchstone relationships. I wonder if those elements could be worked together.</div> </div> </div> </div>My wishes exactly.<br /> <br /> In Vampire and Werewolf, Touchstones kept you anchored to the world. So Touchstones in Changeling should be something similar. While Clarity helps you be grounded on reality, that's a side-effect of being better able to discern better between reality and fantasy. On the other hand, Bargain-pledges made with mortals do tie you to the human community, and court-Bargains tie you to the changeling community. So it seems logical that Touchstones relate to Bargains.<br /> <br /> Of course, we still don't know exactly what the Bargain in the preview is, so all of this could be moot. It really could be just Autumn's particular jargon on &quot;how to protect yourself against the Gentry,&quot; rather than a game mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T02:06:57-07:00","id":1075802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075793#post1075793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My wishes exactly.<br /> <br /> In Vampire and Werewolf, Touchstones kept you anchored to the world. So Touchstones in Changeling should be something similar. While Clarity helps you be grounded on reality, that's a side-effect of being better able to discern better between reality and fantasy. On the other hand, Bargain-pledges made with mortals do tie you to the human community, and court-Bargains tie you to the changeling community. So it seems logical that Touchstones relate to Bargains.<br /> <br /> Of course, we still don't know exactly what the Bargain in the preview is, so all of this could be moot. It really could be just Autumn's particular jargon on &amp;quot;how to protect yourself against the Gentry,&amp;quot; rather than a game mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope that's the case. A Changeling character I've had since the previews started is one that has his Fetch as his Touchstone, as his Keeper removed almost every one of his memories in Arcadia; his Fetch is not only the keeper of what he was, but a piece of what he is, both of them being the &quot;real him&quot; in spite of both being products of Arcadia (one more literal than the other). I'd hate if the Touchstone system was removed, because it'd take a lot of weight off of him not only keeping the Fetch alive but protecting it...and...bleh, it is way too late at night to be elaborating on character motivations without going horribly off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T02:11:16-07:00","id":1075804,"title":"","content":"Speaking of fetches, and remembering an old homebrew content about this fetch character who faked his true identity and became the Autumn King (can't remember whose homebrew was it)<br /> <br /> Can you fake being a changeling to get into a Court?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T06:24:05-07:00","id":1075855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075804#post1075804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of fetches, and remembering an old homebrew content about this fetch character who faked his true identity and became the Autumn King (can't remember whose homebrew was it)<br /> <br /> Can you fake being a changeling to get into a Court?</div> </div> </div> </div> We don't know how Oaths or even the pledge system have changed if at all so its its impossible to know that previously only Changelings and Fae Touched could join courts because only they could participate in oaths although fetches and possibly others could get court good will merit.<br /> <br /> Now who knows (well the devs do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T09:47:52-07:00","id":1075925,"title":"","content":"Touchstones are part of the game, and every character has one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:22:43-07:00","id":1076174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075925#post1075925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones are part of the game, and every character has one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks, that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:39:08-07:00","id":1076547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1074654#post1074654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So... what exactly do you want from these? Extended actions that take longer than Instant action combat abilities? Separate powers? Flexable abilties on the cheap? Exclusivity? Something clearly labeled?<br /> <br /> I'm honestly curious here. What do you feel this ability would be like? And how would it be different from, say, Goblin Vows?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability of having a ritualized Extended Action to make something magic happen. With a set of rules for this thematic approach, like special Glamour costs or Material Costs.<br /> <br /> Like Fairy Tale Bargains for using a spinning wheel to make gold and accquiring a limited amount of resources, but having to power this with Glamour reaped from a mother who just conceived a newborn.<br /> <br /> Or Cursing some rival to fail in a circustance, cause you somehow got a pint of its blood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:42:42-07:00","id":1076581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1076547#post1076547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ability of having a ritualized Extended Action to make something magic happen. With a set of rules for this thematic approach, like special Glamour costs or Material Costs.<br /> <br /> Like Fairy Tale Bargains for using a spinning wheel to make gold and accquiring a limited amount of resources, but having to power this with Glamour reaped from a mother who just conceived a newborn.<br /> <br /> Or Cursing some rival to fail in a circustance, cause you somehow got a pint of its blood.</div> </div> </div> </div> I could see an extended action ritual as away of covering your side of a goblin vow, abit backwards, the magic effect happens first, then the ritual, a quirk that oddly suits Changeling.<br /> <br /> Example Goblin Vow Oak Trees. The Changeling promises to conduct that ancient rite of flaming oak tree in exchange for a magic staff made of oak (token \u2022\u2022\u2022) and gets the staff, and then to keep their end of the bargain does an extended ritual the rite of the burning oak tree until enough successes accrue to met their end of the Goblin Vow.<br /> <br /> Maybe the next day the same changeling does the ritual of the Oak Lion which involves carving a piece of oak into the shape of a lion or singing songs of praise to the Oak Lion as an extended action ritual, with the needed successes depending up duration and the like, which summons a Oak Lion, a Hedge Beast made of Polished Oak in the shape of a lion (Hedge Beast Companion \u2022\u2022\u2022).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-11-2017, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T17:14:52-07:00","id":1076719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075925#post1075925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones are part of the game, and every character has one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they any different from those in Vampire or Werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T20:38:29-07:00","id":1076780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1075925#post1075925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones are part of the game, and every character has one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm assuming they don't have to be connection to one's old life - they can be elements of the new life you're trying to build - they're just something not of Faerie that grounds you and gives you... well... clarity, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T03:37:58-07:00","id":1076891,"title":"","content":"&quot;There are rules for making your own Bargains, Mantles, and Crowns in Chapter 7.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bargains appear to have replaced the Bulwark/Approaches system. Crowns sound more unique to a particular court. Mantles are likely the same, except for changing Approaches for something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T04:04:02-07:00","id":1076893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1076547#post1076547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Stuff</div> </div> </div> </div> Alright. Thank you for satisfying my curiosity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T04:09:20-07:00","id":1076895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073532#post1073532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">perhaps a stretch goal along the lines of <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i>.;</div> </div> </div> </div> Another hint at a possible Changeling 2e Kickstarter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:36:00-07:00","id":1077059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1076780#post1076780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming they don't have to be connection to one's old life - they can be elements of the new life you're trying to build - they're just something not of Faerie that grounds you and gives you... well... clarity, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes!<br /> <br /> For vampires (especially young ones), Touchstones are often backward-looking, because they're a way of maintaining grounding when all of your certainties are being swept away. <i>Changeling</i> is much more about building your own life and self, so Touchstones are about the ways you find to claim your space and identity. Humanity is about maintaining your ability to empathize with people you're increasingly isolated from, while Clarity is about claiming the validity of your own perspective and emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:01:53-07:00","id":1081495,"title":"","content":"Are Court Contracts and the rule that two of your starting contract dots must be invested in them still a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T05:52:16-07:00","id":1081792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1081495#post1081495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Court Contracts and the rule that two of your starting contract dots must be invested in them still a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div> Was that ever a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T05:59:03-07:00","id":1081796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1081792#post1081792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that ever a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Closest was that in 1e two of your contract dots had to be put into seeming contracts or court contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T07:31:51-07:00","id":1081825,"title":"","content":"Oh ok, good t know","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T03:48:56-07:00","id":1082208,"title":"","content":"I'm looking for the new version of the Seasonal Courts. I loved the original Miami setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:39:51-07:00","id":1124409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073083-the-autumn-court-open-development-blog?p=1073532#post1073532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power creation rules that were in earlier drafts are still in the book -- those are the Mantles, as mentioned in the blog post. Some specific mechanics have changed; for example, a +1 bonus to a +2, or a Defense modifier added or removed. If you want Court-specific Contracts for your new Courts, then you'll want to design those yourself -- but that was the case in earlier drafts, as well. (And I think the updated Contract structure is actually going to make that easier than in 1e or earlier drafts, but that's a bit of a tangent.)<br /> <br /> As for a sort of geopolitical look at changeling culture, that'd be an interesting thing for another book -- perhaps a stretch goal along the lines of <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i>. But the models for local Courts are going to be very individual, along the lines of &quot;to the changelings of Reykjavik, seasons have intricate meanings unlike anywhere else in the world,&quot; rather than international, like &quot;Northern Europe has long been under the sorrowful tyranny of the Winter Court.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd love a &quot;Changeling Seed&quot; Collection of courts the world over as a stretch goal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> that would be FANTASTIC!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}